        <body>
            <div xml:id="d113">

                <pb facs="0285" n="1245" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1245"/>

                <head>No. 826.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Whitehouse to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 19, 1888</date>.
                        (Received November 27.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 194.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On Saturday, the 17th instant, I received
                    your telegram in regard to the visit of Major Ernst to El Paso.</p>
                <p>As I was not able to see Mr. Mariscal personally, I sent him early this morning
                    the inclosed note, requesting that he would be kind enough to inform me at his
                    earliest convenience of the appointment of the Mexican engineer detailed to
                    co-operate with Major Ernst.</p>
                <p>On the receipt of the desired information I will wire you an abstract.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Remsen
                    Whitehouse.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d113-a1.xml" xpointer="d113-a1"/>
